    2-5.1  Select Screen Mode (Live Nodes) (V38 Only)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This option allows you to select the screen modes, size, bitplanes with
    an asl requester for all real/live nodes.
    This must be set in order to use Tempest.
    (Supported Locally only)

    * NOTE: If you are running WB 2.04 (v37) then install the v38 Asl.library
            included with the Tempest archive.

    * NOTE!!!!:  Even though the asl requester highlights one of the entires
                 when it opens up, it is NOT really selected, you MUST!!
                 Select it again even if it is highlighted!


    2-5.2  Use Workbench Screen (Live Nodes)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This is whether or not you want Tempest windows to open up on the
    workbench screen or have their own custom screen for Real/Live Nodes.
    Recommended Setting: No


    2-5.3  Auto Iconify At Start Up (Live Nodes)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This setting will determine whether the bbs opens up un-iconified or
    if it is iconified when first loaded for all live nodes.
    Recommended Setting: Yes


    2-5.4  Open Screen Behind Others (Live Nodes)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This setting is only valid if you are opening the bbs in un-iconify
    mode.  When the node is loaded, the window it opens up goes to the back.


    2-5.5  Select Screen Mode (Local Nodes) (V38 Only)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This option allows you to select the screen modes, size, bitplanes to
    use in the bbs with an asl requester for all Local nodes.
    This must be set in order to use Tempest.
    (Supported Locally only)

    * NOTE: If you are running WB 2.04 (v37) then install the v38 Asl.library
            included with the Tempest files.

    * NOTE!!!!:  Even though the asl requester highlights one of the entires
                 when it opens up, it is NOT really selected, you MUST!!
                 Select it again even if it is highlighted!


    2-5.6  Use Workbench Screen (Local Nodes)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This is whether or not you want Tempest windows to open up on the
    workbench screen or have their own customscreen for Local Nodes.
    Recommended Setting: No


    2-5.7  Auto Iconify At Start Up (Live Nodes)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This setting will determine whether the bbs opens up un-iconified or
    if it is iconified when first loaded for all live nodes.
    Recommended Setting: Yes


    2-5.8  Open Screen Behind Others (Live Nodes)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This setting is only valid if you are opening the bbs in un-iconify
    mode.  When the node is loaded, the window it opens up goes to the back.


    2-5.9  Selecting Font
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    There are 3 gadgets.
    1) Allows you to type in the font name.
    2) Allows you to type in the font size.
    3) Opens an asl font requester where you can select a font.
    Recommended to use a font size of 8, so that everything fits nicely.


    2-5.10  Window to Front Options
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This allows you to define whether you want the screen to come to the
    front when 1) a user logs on to the BBS, 2) if a user pages the sysop.
    You can turn them both off, both on, or either one on/off.


    2-5.11  Default ASL Requesters Mode
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    There are 3 modes of operation:

    1) Ask to Use = Y/N Prompt asking you if you want to use asl requesters.
    2) Always Use = Always use asl requesters without asking.
    3) Never  Use = Never use asl requesters, always use input prompt.

    Recommended Setting: Ask to Use


    2-5.12  Half Screen Mode
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This makes Tempest screens open up in half height mode.  Text scrolls
    are faster since it has half the text to scroll, however account editor
    and other operations of the bbs may be impossible since most things are
    based on the regular screen size.
    Recommended setting: Off


