    2-7.1  Password: System Entry
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Password required for a user to enter the BBS.  This is a front end
    password that requires a user to know the password to log on the BBS.
    To disable this password, leave the entry blank.


    2-7.2  Password: New User
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Password required for any new user to apply and fill out an
    application.
    To disable this password, leave the entry blank.


    2-7.3  Password: Sysop Commands
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Password required for sysop(s) and co-sysop(s) to access high level
    sysop related commands.
    To disable this password, leave the entry blank.


    2-7.4  Password: Remote Shell
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Passord required for accessing remote shell and dos commands from the
    BBS.  This password is required!  If the sysop has not defined this
    password then the remote shell and dos commands become inactive.
    Remote Shell is required to have a password no matter what.  This has
    been done for security!


    2-7.5  Password: Local Access
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Password required for a person to do sysop logon, local logon, or
    account editing from the local computer.  This is a password you would
    use if you had friends over or didn't want anyone in your house accessing
    the BBS while you are not around.
    To disable this password, leave the entry blank.


    2-7.6  Password: BBSConfig Module
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Password needed to access the BBSConfig remotely.


    2-7.7  Password: Server Protect
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Password needed to access Server after it has been protected with the
    protect gadget.


    2-7.8  Password: Local Logon
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Password to be used by sysops locally only!.. Lets you logon as any
    user without knowning thier password.


    2-7.9  Attempts: User Handle
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Number of attempts that are allowed for a user to enter their handle
    before the BBS hangs up on user.
    Valid Range: 1-10 attempts.
    Recommended: 3


    2-7.10  Attempts: User Password
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Number of attempts that are allowed on the User Password before the
    BBS hangs up on the user.
    Valid Range: 1-10 attempts.
    Recommended: 3


    2-7.11  Attempts: System Pass
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Number of attempts that are allowed on the System Password before the
    BBS hangs up on the user.
    Valid Range: 1-10 attempts.
    Recommended: 3


    2-7.12  Attempts: NewUser Pass
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Number of attempts that are allowed on the New User Password before the
    BBS hangs up on the user.
    Valid Range: 1-10 attempts.
    Recommended: 3


    2-7.13  Minimum: User Password
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This is the minimum number of characters that a user must enter for a
    password.  If set at 5, for example, the user would have to enter a
    password at least 5 characters long.


    2-7.14  Password (Node Access Password)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This is the password required to logon a certain node.
    Current node is selected above with the Node Scroller gadget.


    2-7.15  Minimum Access (Node Minimum Access Level)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    This is the minimum access level a user must have to logon a certain
    node.
    Current node is selected above with the Node Scroller gadget.


